#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171710 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172130 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5256297-c928-54e3-bf4d-35f5734f5632" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing Surface Integrals Over Parametric Surfaces"}] :question/id #uuid "38dc8ce4-246d-54bd-a400-48c801d9387f" :question/math-academy-id "e-12344" :question/problem "![](images/6a/6ad2702c610c5e7d31d07584c6e605467ff25c8474befd433214451169cc1180.png)\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z) = z-y$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u^2, \\: -v, \\: v \\big\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v) \\in D \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^2,$ where $u \\geq 0.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $\\| \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\| = 2\\sqrt{2}u.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n\\| \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\| = 2\\sqrt{2}u.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(z-y)\\,{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=-v\\,z=v} \\\\  & =v-(-v) \\\\  & =2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,4\\sqrt{2}uv\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171711 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b529430-3406-506c-b67d-c067dfee44d5" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Surface Integrals Over Parametric Surfaces"}] :question/id #uuid "fce43073-3f48-5e12-a5c0-ecef3a31a57a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12346" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{S} (x-y)\\: \\textrm{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx = u+v, \\qquad \ny = u-v, \\qquad \nz = v\n$$\n\nfor $0 \\leq u \\leq 3$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 3.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u+v, \\: u-v, \\: v\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =x-y\\,{|}_{x=u+v\\,y=u-v\\,z=v} \\\\  & =(u+v)-(u-v) \\\\  & =2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD = \\{ (u,v) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq u \\leq 3, \\: 0 \\leq v \\leq 3\\},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}(x-y)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2v\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{∬}_{D}\\,2v\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2v\\,\\text{d}v\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}1\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot [{v}^{2}]_{0}^{3}\\cdot [u]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot 9\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =27\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172130 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5256297-c928-54e3-bf4d-35f5734f5632" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing Surface Integrals Over Parametric Surfaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a6318e5-3878-5d26-b61b-739d349729a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({u}^{2}+u)v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275566} {:answer/id #uuid "2913e3a7-4834-5ae0-8725-8cf0ddd19bbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({u}^{2}+uv+{u}^{2})v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275848} {:answer/id #uuid "4635f4d0-2e93-54c6-a194-c7414540fea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276098} {:answer/id #uuid "8e7629cd-993c-5b5b-a5b5-4827bb2f0380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276769} {:answer/id #uuid "fa861672-33f6-547e-b490-0aa338df3abc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(u+v)v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a6318e5-3878-5d26-b61b-739d349729a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({u}^{2}+u)v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275566} :answer-field/id #uuid "758915d5-fc00-56c4-ac7b-2a8b40d5ac5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a99cdea7-3ae5-5a3e-abca-eaac3de706cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-160712" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=x+y+z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,u-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=2v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(x+y+z)\\,{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=u-{v}^{2}\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+(u-{v}^{2})+{v}^{2} \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2({u}^{2}+u)v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b529430-3406-506c-b67d-c067dfee44d5" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Surface Integrals Over Parametric Surfaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bea4b28f-ce09-5500-9439-8c3c8b7ee3cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169126} {:answer/id #uuid "ce545157-bc0c-5334-bc0e-9135235b5624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169127} {:answer/id #uuid "d0a0829c-6ceb-5f41-9889-8a865432b8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169128} {:answer/id #uuid "fd45b78a-7e91-59f5-a92a-3f200b6d2bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169129} {:answer/id #uuid "2581dec6-23e3-515e-92fb-d7811092bcb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169130}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6fc03f50-c767-57bd-8d63-af287106c460" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169125}] :question/id #uuid "82d5af65-9d79-5b70-b0f6-be91c0743951" :question/math-academy-id "q-160834" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n$∬_(S)(2x + y + z)dS$,\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n$r(u, v) = ⟨2u - v, 3u + 2, u + 2v⟩$\nover the domain $D = {(u, v): 0 \\le u \\le 1,-1 \\le v \\le 1}$.\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′}‖ = \\sqrt{70}$.*"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172378 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b529430-3406-506c-b67d-c067dfee44d5" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Surface Integrals Over Parametric Surfaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5a1c5c4-aaff-5dad-85ae-7c455c4e77b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169132} {:answer/id #uuid "ad5264d6-51e2-571c-a97d-f200747b780d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169133} {:answer/id #uuid "d262b1ed-6abf-5731-aad7-a59edbd4996a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169134} {:answer/id #uuid "033ce6a7-bfa6-5c47-acc2-cddc0cab717e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169135} {:answer/id #uuid "2814803c-3a0a-59a5-b8f2-9a2b1d57c431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169136}] :answer-field/id #uuid "126dc10e-27a9-5d7d-894d-84b3d2d7de05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169131}] :question/id #uuid "588db1ad-67d5-5fad-b786-e13158fbed5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-160835" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n$∬_(S)4xydS$,\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n$x = u, y = v, z = 6 - 3u - 2v$\nfor $0 \\le u \\le 2$ and $0 \\le v \\le 3$."}]}
